  "foaf:name": "Marine Data Exchange: Heritage Accelerator",
  "sdo:name": "Marine Data Exchange: Heritage Accelerator",
  "sdo:description": "The Marine Data Exchange Heritage Accelerator (MDEHA) is an innovative project on heritage information generated by marine development in England’s seas. The data remobilised by this project will help project-specific and strategic decision-making to achieve net zero through offshore wind expansion. It will help facilitate cleaner energy as well as share knowledge about marine heritage. When offshore wind farms and other forms of marine development are being planned and constructed, the results of geophysical and geotechnical surveys are used to provide information about heritage to avoid or reduce impacts. Although very detailed, this information is not easy to find and use. The MDEHA project will recapture heritage information from seabed surveys over the past 20 years and transfer it into archives and databases within The Crown Estate’s Marine Data Exchange (MDE) and Historic England’s National Marine Heritage Record (NMHR) where it can be more easily discovered and explored.",
